	The file or directory is part of the operating system or is used exclusively by the operating system.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDirectory</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY.The handle identifies a directory.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bArchive</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ARCHIVE. The file or directory is an archive file or directory.
	Applications use this attribute to mark files for backup or removal.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDevice</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DEVICE. Under CE: FILE_ATTRIBUTE_INROM or FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ENCRYPTED ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bNormal</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL. The file or directory has no other attributes set. This attribute is valid only if used alone.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTemporary</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_TEMPORARY. The file is being used for temporary storage.
	File systems attempt to keep all of the data in memory for quicker access, rather than flushing it back to mass storage. 
	A temporary file should be deleted by the application as soon as it is no longer needed.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSparseFile</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_SPARSE_FILE. The file is a sparse file.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bReparsePoint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT. The file has an associated reparse point.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCompressed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_COMPRESSED. The file or directory is compressed.
	For a file, this means that all of the data in the file is compressed. 
	For a directory, this means that compression is the default for newly created files and subdirectories.]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bOffline</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FILE_ATTRIBUTE_OFFLINE. Under CE: FILE_ATTRIBUTE_ROMSTATICREF. The file data is not immediately available.
